@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix vdv: <https://hexplain.io/ns/video#> .

<https://hexplain.io/ns/video> skos:scopeNote "Use for video containers, streams, tracks and timing metadata. Nominal rate must not be used as an exact variable-rate timeline."@en .
vdv:Interlaced skos:definition "Scanning convention in which successive fields carry different line subsets of an image frame."@en .
vdv:PositiveAspectRatioShape rdfs:label "Positive Aspect Ratio Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to subjects using vdv:aspectRatio. Both aspect-ratio components must be positive."@en .
vdv:Progressive skos:definition "Scanning convention in which a frame represents a full image rather than alternating interlaced fields."@en .
vdv:RateShape rdfs:label "Rate Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to subjects using vdv:frameRateDenominator, vdv:frameRateNumerator. vdv:frameRateDenominator takes exactly one value, an xsd:integer or xsd:positiveInteger literal greater than 0. vdv:frameRateNumerator takes exactly one value, an xsd:integer or xsd:positiveInteger literal greater than 0."@en .
vdv:StreamShape rdfs:label "Stream Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of vdv:VideoStream, vdv:VideoTrack; subjects using vdv:aspectRatio, vdv:audioChannels, vdv:frameCount, vdv:frameRate, vdv:frameRateDenominator, vdv:frameRateNumerator, vdv:scanType. acolor:colorSpace takes at most one value; each is an IRI naming an instance of skos:Concept. aenc:bitrate takes at most one value; each is a number greater than 0. aenc:codec takes at most one value; each is an IRI naming an instance of skos:Concept. araster:height takes at most one value; each is a number greater than 0. araster:width takes at most one value; each is a number greater than 0. atime:duration takes at most one value; each is an xsd:decimal or xsd:integer literal at least 0. vdv:aspectRatio takes at most one value; each is an xsd:string literal matching the regular expression ^[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?:[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?$. vdv:audioChannels takes at most one value; each is an xsd:integer or xsd:positiveInteger literal greater than 0. vdv:frameCount takes at most one value; each is an xsd:integer or xsd:unsignedLong literal at least 0, at most 18446744073709551615. vdv:frameRate takes at most one value; each is an xsd:decimal or xsd:integer literal greater than 0. vdv:scanType takes at most one value; each is either vdv:Progressive or vdv:Interlaced."@en .
vdv:VideoContainer skos:definition "A containing resource for one or more video streams and associated tracks or metadata."@en .
vdv:VideoStream skos:definition "An ordered video sequence with timing and display properties independent of its container encoding."@en .
vdv:VideoTrack skos:definition "A container-level track carrying a video sequence; track identity is distinct from individual frames."@en .
vdv:audioChannels skos:definition "The declared number of audio channels associated with the video resource."@en .
vdv:axisFrame skos:definition "Deprecated duplicate of dlv:axisTime for successive video frames, kept so existing descriptions resolve."@en .
vdv:frameCount skos:definition "The declared number of frames in a video sequence; it does not by itself establish duration for variable-rate material."@en .
vdv:frameRate skos:definition "The nominal number of frames per second expressed as a decimal or integer value. Exact non-terminating rational rates require the numerator/denominator properties."@en .
vdv:scanType skos:definition "The scanning convention used to organize image lines into frames or fields."@en .
